$DATUM To a solution of compound 10 (2.84 g, 5.04 mmol) and Bu3SnH (5.09 g, 17.5
mmol) in toluene (40 ml) at reflex under Ar was added a solution of AIBN
(0.17 g, 1.0 mmol) in toluene (6 ml). The reaction mixture was stirred at
reflux for 30 min and cooled to room temperature. The mixture was
concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude product was purified by
silica gel column chromatography (hexane/ethyl acetate = 14:1). Yield:
(2.01 g, 97%) as a white crystalline. [a]D26 -22.6 (c 0.54, CHCl3); IR
(KBr) 2964, 2934, 2856, 1778, 1429, 1164, 1113, 1094, 1065, 825, 702
cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 1.05 (s, 9H), 1.23 (s, 3H), 2.08 (d, J =
14.7 Hz, 1H), 2.57 (dd, J = 14.7, 6.4 Hz, 1H), 2.70 (d, J = 2.9 Hz, 2H),
3.40 (d, J = 10.5 Hz, 1H), 3.61 (d, J = 10.5 Hz, 1H), 4.85 (ddd, J = 4.6,
2.9, 2.9 Hz, 1H), 5.08 (dd, J = 6.4, 4.6 Hz, 1H), 7.37-7.46 (m, 6H),
7.63-7.66 (m, 4H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 19.2, 24.4, 26.8, 37.5,
39.9, 70.6, 79.3, 85.9, 86.3, 127.7, 127.8, 129.8, 129.9, 132.9, 133.0,
135.5, 135.5, 175.8.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stereoselective Formation of Tetrahydrofuran Rings via [3 + 2]
Annulation: Total Synthesis of Plakortone L
