$DATUM (4aR,5aS,9aS,10aS)-Octahydro-4a-methoxy-1H,3H,5aH-dithiopyrano[4,3-b:3',4'-e]pyran
(13c). Tributylstannane (0.28mL, 1.0 mmol) was added to a stirred
solution of xanthate (300mg, 0.82 mmol) in dry toluene (5 mL) under
argon. The mixture was heated under reflux and then AIBN (ca. 10 mg) was
added. After 30 min, the reaction was allowed to cool to ambient
temperature and then was diluted with H2O and extracted with CH2Cl2. The
combined organic layers were dried over Na2SO4, concentrated, and the
resulting colorless oil was passed through a short pad of silica gel
(eluting first with hexane and then with 5%ethyl acetate in hexane) to
afford the titled product (195 mg, 91%). [α]D -40, (c 0.7, benzene); IR
νmax: 2922,2826, 1420, 1325, 1211, 1104, 1044, 942, 882 cm-1; 1H NMR (500
MHz, C6D6) δ: 3.63 (1H, ddd, J = 3, 3, 3 Hz,HC-5a), 3.00 (1H, dd, J =
12.5, 13 Hz), 2.89 (1H, ddd, J = 3, 13, 13 Hz), 2.79 (1H, dd, J = 11.5,
12 Hz), 2.74 (3H,s, H3CO), 2.68 (1H, ddd, J = 3, 13.5, 13.5 Hz), 2.05
(1H, dddd, J = 2, 4, 4, 13 Hz), 1.97 (1H, dddd, J = 2, 4, 4, 13Hz), 1.95
(1H, ddd, J = 3, 3, 14 Hz), 1.89-1.73 (4H, m), 1.66-1.51 (4H, m), 0.71
(1H, ddd, J = 2, 4, 13 Hz); 13CNMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 98.6 (s, C-4a),
66.1 (d, C-5a), 46.4 (q, CH3O), 41.4 (d), 37.0 (d), 34.2 (t), 33.6 (t),
32.6(t), 31.2 (t), 27.4 (t), 25.7 (t), 23.0 (t); LRMS (EI), m/z (relative
intensity): 260 ([M]+, 91), 229 (47), 228 (85),195 (25), 141 (25), 139
(21), 113 (100), 99 (28), 79 (27); HRMS m/z calcd for C12H20O2S2
260.0905, found 260.0898.
