$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A mixture of the acetonide (0.154 g, 0.184 mmol), Ph3SnH (0.097 g, 0.276
mmol), and AIBN (0.006 g, 0.037 mmol) was brought to reflux. More Ph3SnH
(0.097 g, 0.276 mmol), and AIBN (0.006 g, 0.037 mmol) were added every 2
h. After being stirred at reflux for 6 h, the solution was cooled and
concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by flash chromatography
(5:1 Hex/EA) to give alkene 2 (0.121 g, 0.165 mmol) in 90% yield as a
colorless oil. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ 1.10 (d, J = 6.5 Hz, 3H), 1.14
(m, 1H), 1.15 (d, J = 6.3 Hz, 3H), 1.34 (s, 3H), 1.40 (s, 3H), 1.70 (m,
1H), 1.78 (dt, J = 10.2, 6.7 Hz, 1H), 1.95 (ddd, J = 13.4, 4.3, 1.9 Hz,
1H), 2.14 (m, 1H), 2.36 (dt, J = 10.2, 4.4 Hz, 1H), 2.89 (app t, J = 9.9
Hz, 1H), 3.07 (app t, J = 9.8 Hz, 1H), 3.27 (ddd, J = 11, 7.5, 1.8 Hz,
1H), 3.49 (ddd, J = 10.5, 7, 3.6 Hz, 1H), 3.78 (s, 3H), 3.79 (s, 3H),
3.90 (m, 3H), 4.05 (m, 1H), 4.55 (ABq, J = 10.1 Hz, ΔυAB = 56.2 Hz, 2H),
4.58 (ABq, J = 10.6 Hz, ΔυAB = 32.7 Hz, 2H), 4.63 (tt, J = 5.7, 1.6 Hz,
1H), 5.00 (dd, J = 11.1, 5.8 Hz, 1H), 5.36 (dt, J = 17.6, 1.7 Hz, 1H),
